<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_Breaklight.xml                     UtinniPatches · GREENTIDE_MECHANICS_2 M5
  ============================================================================
  greentide_kit_spec.md "M5. Breaklight — clarity as the disaster": "a rare
  IncidentDef-triggered RM_GameCondition_EnvironmentalWeather... condition
  preset." Fires Defs/GameConditionDefs/RUT_BreaklightCondition.xml.

  category=Misc, workerClass=IncidentWorker_MakeGameCondition (or a thin
  subclass of it): confirmed against the live def dump this pass
  (mcp__rimsage__get_def_details HeatWave, raw) that vanilla's own weather-
  event incidents (HeatWave, ColdSnap) use exactly this shape — category
  Misc, baseChance + minRefireDays, no bespoke StorytellerComp — so Breaklight
  rides the Storyteller's ordinary periodic Misc-incident roll rather than a
  hand-rolled MapComponent timer (contrast RUT_Surge.xml, which deliberately
  bans ANY schedule field for a different biome's own "no clockwork tide"
  rule — no such ban exists in this kit spec's M5 section).

  workerClass=RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RUT_IncidentWorker_Breaklight
  (this pass's own new class, EnvironmentalHazards Source/): a one-line
  subclass of vanilla's own IncidentWorker_MakeGameCondition adding only the
  MOD_OPTIONS_RETROFIT_1 settings gate (breaklightEnabled) — no firing logic
  of its own. See that class's own header for why a bespoke subclass was
  needed here (a permanent biomeMapConditions lock has no equivalent
  toggle-hook gap; a rare incident does).

  baseChance 1 / minRefireDays 6: both this pass's own INVENTED-BUILD values
  — the spec names a duration (3-8 hours, on the condition/IncidentDef pair
  below) but no refire cadence. allowedBiomes=[RUT_Greentide] makes baseChance
  effectively "this biome's own share of the Misc queue," same posture
  RUT_Surge.xml's own header already explains for allowedBiomes generally
  (CanFireNow enforces it even off a Storyteller-driven roll, verified
  against the live decompile there).

  durationDays 0.125~0.3333 = 3-8 in-game hours, the spec's own INVENTED
  figure converted to the days unit IncidentWorker_MakeGameCondition.
  TryExecuteWorker actually consumes — same conversion RUT_Surge.xml's own
  header already documents for its own duration figure.

  MayRequire is load-bearing: workerClass and gameCondition both resolve
  into mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards content.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <IncidentDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_Breaklight</defName>
    <label>Breaklight</label>
    <targetTags>
      <li>Map_PlayerHome</li>
    </targetTags>
    <category>Misc</category>
    <workerClass>RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RUT_IncidentWorker_Breaklight</workerClass>
    <gameCondition>RUT_BreaklightCondition</gameCondition>
    <durationDays>0.125~0.3333</durationDays>
    <baseChance>1</baseChance>
    <minRefireDays>6</minRefireDays>
    <allowedBiomes>
      <li>RUT_Greentide</li>
    </allowedBiomes>
    <letterLabel>Breaklight</letterLabel>
    <letterDef>NegativeEvent</letterDef>
  </IncidentDef>

</Defs>
